# Silhouette outline (client/MANIFEST.md "game_cosmeticfx", server/README.md "Footprints and outlines"): Creature:setOutline(r, g, b, a, widthPx, pulseMs), setOutlineGradient(r, g, b, a) (the colour at the top, a vertical gradient), clearOutline() and hasOutline() for Lua. The outfit queues one outline item under its mount and body parts (addons, rider, the walking frame) and draws it from their final rects: each part once more as a quad grown by the width, through a program that samples the part's alpha in a ring of 8 directions and paints where the part is transparent and a neighbour is not. The parts draw over it, so only the outer contour of the whole silhouette stays; outfit shaders, wings, auras, names and bars are not touched. The width is in sprite pixels times the sprite size factor (HD upscaling, patch 0027). On the map for every creature with an outline; in a widget only for the widget's own preview creature (id 0), never for map creatures shown in lists. Touches only outfit.h/.cpp, creature.h/.cpp and luafunctions_client.cpp.
